  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\cos ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{y}{b}\\right)=\\log \\left(\\frac{x}{n}\\right)^{n}$. Then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$x^{2} y_{2}+x y_{1}+n^{2} y=0$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$x y_{2}-x y_{1}+2 n^{2} y=0$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$x^{2} y_{2}+3 x y_{1}-n^{2} y=0$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$x y_{2}+5 x y_{1}-3 y=0$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint:\r\n$\\cos ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{y}{b}\\right)=\\log \\left(\\frac{x}{n}\\right)^{n}=n \\times \\log \\left(\\frac{x}{n}\\right)$\r\n$\\Rightarrow-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{b^{2}-y^{2}}} \\cdot y_{1}=\\frac{n}{x}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow x^{2} y_{1}^{2}=n^{2}\\left(b^{2}-y^{2}\\right) \\Rightarrow x^{2} y_{2}+x y_{1}+n^{2} y=0$"
  }
}